          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Expedition of the Thousand</strong><br>\nIn 1860, Garibaldi led the legendary Expedition of the Thousand in Sicily and Naples, which was a critical step in the unification process. With a volunteer army, he won astonishing victories and handed control over to King Victor Emmanuel II.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Life and Politics</strong><br>\nAfter the unification, Garibaldi was elected to the Italian parliament but remained at odds with the monarchy's policies. He continued to advocate for democratic reforms and social justice.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Franco-Prussian War</strong><br>\nDuring the Franco-Prussian War, Garibaldi led a group of volunteers to support France against Prussia in 1870. His internationalism and belief in the cause of freedom overrode national boundaries.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
